        <mxCell id="legend_text" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#15202B;fontSize=16;align=left;" value="&lt;b&gt;Notation:&lt;/b&gt; Role = circle with lower curve; Goal = oval; Task = hexagon; Resource = rectangle. T-head at parent = AND (child &amp;rarr; parent).&lt;br&gt;A Goal Dependency has an external goal dependum between two D-marked legs, directed from Auction (depender) to the responsible Role (dependee). It expresses expected fulfilment and allows failure.&lt;br&gt;participates-in relates actors; it does not replace goal dependencies. Mission/norm labels trace MOISE allocation. Administrative goalSatisfied(bid) does not establish actual bidding or normative root achievement." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="80" y="1253" width="2600" height="74" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
